      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · Peau noire, masques blancs, chapter I (French text, PDF pp.36–56)",
          "title": "Speaking opens access and installs a measure",
          "italic": "The scene demonstrates the double movement: real acquisition, and the alienation that can accompany it — the mask is socially effective because it can do something.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The Antillean speaker enters a language whose social authority precedes his arrival. Speech is heard through education, prestige and institutional authority; a sentence can secure a hearing because of the world it signals as well as what it says. The inherited whole places real acquisition at the beginning: linguistic skill opens capacities of participation, and treating it as an empty disguise would erase those capacities. But the authority attached to the skill",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "can become a rule for self-evaluation: the speaker begins to hear himself through the standard by which the dominant world hears him. The movement can also change his relation to others — an inward criterion used to judge those whose speech does not satisfy it, reproducing the distribution of prestige. The difference between capacity and its social valuation is indispensable: one can retain what was learned while disputing the hierarchy that claims authority over it.\n\nOccurrences: the acquired skill and its prestige (#1); the inward criterion (#1, deepened at #3); the reproduction of the hierarchy (#1, #3).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
