      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#3 · the title-field; persona and chameleon kept distinct",
          "title": "The mask becomes an inward criterion",
          "italic": "The mask embodies the passage from participation into self-administration — the whole cannot end by peeling a surface to reveal an untouched essence beneath.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The title's white mask gathers the pressure of appearing through a world that distributes recognisable humanity unevenly. It cannot be confined to intentional pretending: a subject may become accomplished in the forms through which the dominant world recognises him while the standard of recognition becomes a rule for administering his own life — the social relation acting through judgements that can feel like his own. The source field joins language, culture, desire and self-image: not four detachable masks, but ways the same hierarchy becomes",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "consequential — speech concerns being heard, self-image how one becomes available to oneself, recognition the response through which another affirms or withholds value. The double edge remains: a legible form opens participation, and participation reinforces the measure admission depended on. The person has not become unreal; what requires examination is the relation by which a contingent measure stands as the condition of value. Jungian persona and the lived chameleon image retain their own histories; the racial-colonial relation owns this whole.\n\nOccurrences: the recognising forms and their mastery (#1, #3); the inward administration (#3); the refused surface/essence ending (#3, #4).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
