      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#5→0 · the four inherited flags; the cross-whole ledger; the source standing",
          "title": "The historical person remains available to answer",
          "italic": "The return keeps the whole load-bearing: a mask without its world is a portable symbol of disguise; a world without the person's capacity to answer makes its classifications final.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The mask can return to the scene that made it meaningful: language carried a prestige hierarchy; the racial hail returned the body through inherited stories; the mask could become a criterion of self-administration; recognition required the social relation itself to become revisable. Removing any movement changes the image's force. The four inherited comparisons keep their unratified standing — mask as adaptive interface, category before encounter, Objective Co-Internality, idol/image — each with its return route named and none promoted by the permission to develop the whole. The cross-whole neighbours stay distinct:",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Number Six's fictional designation differs from a historically reproduced racial schema; Apollo–Daphne's erotic pursuit differs from colonial racial power; the moving mirror adds machine-mediated recursion; Attica's binding determination differs from an already-imposed hierarchy. The primary proposed return is A27 — recognition where the other's reality cannot be exhausted by a prior image — a project synthesis, human-amplified: no. The source standing holds: complete introduction, chapters I, V, VII and conclusion admitted from the French electronic text; English translation selection and quotation collation remain separate.\n\nDeclared cross-story: The Prisoner, the Ovidian Daphne, the moving mirror and Attica as named comparisons with their differences carried. ↳ Occurrences: the four scenes' retention (#0–#4, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
